  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The structures of the oxides of nitrogen&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> &nbsp;are as follows:&nbsp;<br />The oxide molecules of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> ,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> &nbsp;have nitrogen - nitrogen bond in their structure. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></math> has nitrogen-oxygen-nitrogen bond in its structure.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0132_40fdb81c81ca.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 133px;\" /></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 106px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
